jobs.description:
Are you ready to make an impact in one of the largest warehouses in the Benelux? In this role, you will work at a brand-new, large-scale site that is currently undergoing significant development. The operation is growing rapidly, many new colleagues are joining, and processes are being further built and refined. This requires strong supervisors who can bring structure, direction, and clarity to the operation.

As a Warehouse Supervisor, you are the key link between the team leaders on the floor and the warehouse manager. You will indirectly lead a large group of employees and ensure that daily operations run smoothly, efficiently, and according to agreed standards. You will work in an environment where structure is essential and processes must be strictly followed from A to Z. At the same time, you are the one who maintains oversight, makes adjustments, and takes decisions when necessary.

Your responsibilities:

- Leading and supporting multiple team leaders and their teams;
- Monitoring daily operations, planning, and performance;
- Conducting conversations regarding absenteeism, performance, and employee development;
- Justifying operational decisions towards warehouse management (such as capacity and overtime);
- Ensuring strict adherence to processes and procedures;
- Monitoring KPIs, quality, and operational progress;
- Coordinating with different departments and internal stakeholders;
- Identifying bottlenecks and implementing improvements ;
- Working with reports and administrative processes (including Excel).

For this position, we are looking for a strong and experienced supervisor who is used to working in a high-paced, operational warehouse environment.

- Minimum of 3 years’ experience in a leadership role within a logistics or warehouse environment. Experience in retail or supermarkets is not considered relevant for this role;
- Fluent in English (required);
- Experience with Excel and reporting;
- Available full-time (40 hours per week) in a 2-shi

Are you an experienced forklift operator who feels right at home in a logistics environment? Would you like to work for a stable organization where you’ll work alongside a small, close-knit team to ensure everything runs smoothly? Then we have a great opportunity for you!

For a client in Weert, we’re looking for an experienced forklift operator who enjoys working a 3-shift schedule. You’ll be joining a large logistics company where safety, teamwork, and a pleasant work atmosphere are key priorities.

What will you be doing?

As a forklift operator, you’ll be responsible for moving goods efficiently and safely within the warehouse. You’ll spend most of your workday operating the forklift. Together with four colleagues, you’ll ensure that all pallets and goods are placed in the correct locations and that outgoing orders are ready on time.

Your duties will include:

- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Picking orders and preparing them for shipment;
- Scanning goods;
- Moving pallets and goods within the warehouse;
- Preparing outgoing orders for transport.

You'll be operating a forklift with double forks, loading from the side. Do you have experience with this? If so, be sure to read on! 

You’ve already gained considerable experience operating a forklift and understand how important it is to work safely and accurately. You’re flexible, keep a cool head during busy periods, and are comfortable working shifts.

In addition:

- You have at least 1 year of experience as a forklift operator;
- You hold a valid forklift operator’s certificate;
- You are fluent in Dutch or English;
- You are available full-time;
- You work with precision and always put safety first.

Hands-on work, teamwork, and food production. Become a production worker in the food sector in Horst. Stable job, modern working environment, and plenty of growth opportunities!
Bij welk bedrijf ga je aan de slag als Production WorkerAs a Food Production Worker in Horst, you will work at an international family-owned company specializing in the processing and packaging of fresh food products. From a modern and temperature-controlled working environment in Horst, the team works daily on quality, efficiency, and collaboration.
Wat ga je doen als Production WorkerAs a Food Production Worker in Horst, you will work in a dynamic production environment where you are responsible for sorting, processing, and packaging food products according to set guidelines. Together with your colleagues on the production line, you ensure a smooth, efficient, and hygienic production process. You monitor product quality, identify any deviations, and actively contribute to optimizing the process.

You will work in rotating shifts: an early shift from Monday to Saturday, starting at 6:00 AM and typically finishing at 2:00 PM, with possible extension until 3:30 PM. In addition, there is a (late) day shift from Monday to Friday, starting at 12:00 PM and continuing until production is completed. During busier periods, the start time may shift to 2:00 PM.
Wat wij vragen - Good communication skills and you speak English (Dutch or Polish is a plus);
 - You are stress-resistant, enjoy working in a team, and can switch tasks quickly;
 - You have no objection to working in a refrigerated environment;
 - You are willing to work overtime during peak season;
 - You are flexible with working hours (including working every other Saturday).

